      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Small-scale metal fabricators may not be subject to most EPA carbon mandates if your facility's total output is below the significant threshold (typically 25,000 or 100,000 metric tons of CO₂ annually). If you do exceed these limits, the consequences could include mandatory compliance reporting or the imposition of specific emission caps and potential fines for non-compliance. Many small operations avoid these burdens by focusing on the \"significant source\" exemption while still proactively adopting energy efficiency practices to stay well clear of any future rule changes.",
